      "message": "Could you modify the description as follows? And could you give self +1 or +2 to this CL?\n```GraphicsTracker: do not cancelBuffer after stopping\n\nWhen two codecs are using the same surface as below scenario, a buffer in Codec #2 can go inconsistent. Eventually the process using Codec #2 will be aborted. Fix this by not calling cancelBuffer() after GraphicsTracker is stopped.\nCodec #1: stop using the surface (disconnect)\nCodec #2: start to use the surface. (connect)\nCodec #1: cancelBuffer() to the surface in HAL block dtor\nCodec #2: a buffer by dequeueBuffer() is gone mistakenly by 3```",
